    "materials": [
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": "### Passage 1\n\nOne of the most important gifts parents can give their kids is time to play. Finding time to play with kids can be a challenge if parents are busy. But play is not an option, but a must. It is so important to child development that it has been recognized by the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights as a right of every child.\n\nScientists say 75 percent of the brain develops after a baby is born, in the years between birth and the early 20s. Play in childhood motivates the brain to make connections between neurons (神经元). Play during the teen years and into adulthood helps the brain develop even more connectivity. This helps a child or a teenager develop both physical and social skills. Besides, play can also help to increase emotional well-being.\n\nStudies have shown that kids who are encouraged to use their imagination are more creative in their adult life. So it is wise for parents to shut down the screens and encourage their kids to do free play. Free play costs parents nothing but offers kids everything. Throw a sheet over the table to make a lovely tent; hand out paper plates and challenge everyone to make a funny hat; play hide-and-seek with the little ones, etc. All the free play is unstructured, but it makes kids learn important social skills by working with others."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": "### Passage 2\n\nThe number of giraffes is becoming smaller across Africa, according to the Giraffe Conservation Foundation (CCF). The total population has dropped by 40 percent in the last 15 years. The CCF is the only non-governmental organization (NGO) in the world to focus solely on the conservation of giraffes in Africa and is pioneering a sustainable future for this mammal. According to a study, giraffes are quietly disappearing because it is difficult for them to find acacia trees, their favourite food.\n\nWork towards their conservation is more important now than it has ever been. And more and more giraffes are also being hunted. Because of this, the CCF decided to work with African parks. These parks are very important for keeping Nubian giraffes safe. GPS collars were used to keep an eye on giraffes but they cannot stay on for long.\n\nTo solve this problem, new tracking devices which are as small as a chocolate bar, solar-powered and do not bother giraffes much are used to stop illegal hunting and keep giraffes safe."
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "items": [
