      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": "### Passage 1\n\nIt was on Sunday morning, when Sam went to see his grandfather alone. He took the bus to his grandfather's house, as it was quite a distance away. As the bus traveled along, it stopped at a busy stop and a crowd of passengers boarded, including an old lady.\n\nThe bus was already crowded, and there were no more seats available. The old lady looked tired and strained, but she held on to the handrail for support. Sam noticed this and felt a bit uneasy, but he was also far from having an empty seat and could not offer one to her.\n\nSuddenly, a voice came from the back of the bus. It was the little girl, who had boarded the bus before. \"Please, take my seat, Grandma,\" she said sweetly. The old lady was taken aback but soon smiled gratefully and sat down.\n\nThis act of kindness did not just move the old lady. Other passengers, inspired by the little girl, also got up and offered their seats to those who needed them. The atmosphere in the bus suddenly changed from one kind of indifference to one kind of kindness and compassion.\n\nSam watched the scene with a sense of awe. He was amazed by the little girl's selflessness and generosity. It made him realize that true kindness comes from the heart, regardless of age or size.\n\nAs the bus continued its journey, Sam could not help but think about the little girl's act of kindness. He turned to the passenger next to him and said, \"What a lovely little girl!\" Indeed, her simple yet profound act of giving had left a lasting impression on everyone on the bus."
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
